    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48-a1">

                <pb facs="0144" n="1104" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1104"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 244.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morris to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington, D. C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 6,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: As attorney for Mr. Howard C. Walker,
                    I have the honor to transmit to you herewith a petition of Mr. Walker, setting
                    forth the wrongs which he has suffered at the hands of officials of the
                    Government of Mexico, As a citizen of the United States Mr. Walker respectfully
                    claims redress through your Department. Will you he pleased that such steps be
                    taken in the premises as may seem just and proper.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. F. Morris.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
